{
  "id": "COMPOUND:9422 - PROTEIN:810",
  "verbalization": "Tepoxalin is implicated in the activation of the Adenosine receptor A1 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Tepoxalin acts as a target for multiple compounds, all of which are known to interact with the Kappa-type opioid receptor. These compounds—2,4,6-Trimethoxyaniline, Ibipinabant, and 3-Methylthiofentanyl—each have a known target of the Adenosine receptor A1. This implies that Tepoxalin may share a common mechanism of action, possibly through the Kappa-type opioid receptor, which is a key mediator in the activation of the Adenosine receptor A1. The consistent presence of this pathway across different compounds supports the hypothesis that Tepoxalin may also interact with the Adenosine receptor A1 via a similar mechanism, potentially through the Kappa-type opioid receptor. The integration of these findings highlights a possible role for Tepoxalin in modulating the Adenosine receptor A1, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm this relationship.",
